  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food crisis response in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adeso&#x2019;s response will focus on severely drought affected populations in villages within Iskushuban and Banderbeyla districts of Bari region. In these locations, water is extremely scarce, particularly for the remote and pastoral communities that the project is targeting. In addition the body condition of livestock is very poor, which has resulted in low sales of livestock, negatively affecting household purchasing power. The project aims to enhance water supply and access for personal consumption, hygiene and sanitation through cash for water and hygiene promotion for 662 households, and improved food security and livelihoods through three rounds of unconditional cash transfer for 700 households.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AFRICAN DEVELOPMENT SOLUTIONS</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adeso is an African-led humanitarian and development organization that is changing the way people think about and deliver aid in Africa. Since our founding in 1991 as Horn Relief, we have worked with thousands of vulnerable and marginalized communities to assist them in reaching their full potential. Based on this, we have grown rapidly, from a local grassroots NGO operating exclusively in Somalia to a major player on the regional stage, with 15 field offices in Somalia, Kenya and South Sudan and over 200
staff serving communities.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
